@@ -1 +1,23 @@
 # zj — a small JSON toolkit for the command line
+
+A strict JSON validator, formatter and query tool written in Zig (standard library only).
+
+## Build
+
+```
+zig build          # produces zig-out/bin/zj
+zig build test     # runs the unit tests
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+zj validate [FILE]
+zj fmt   [--indent N] [--sort-keys] [--ascii] [FILE]
+zj min   [--sort-keys] [--ascii] [FILE]
+zj query [--raw] [--sort-keys] [--ascii] PATH [FILE]
+```
+
+Input comes from `FILE` or stdin. Paths look like `.users[*].emails[0]`, `.a["b c"][-1]` or `.`.
+Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 invalid JSON (`error: <source>:<line>:<column>: <message>`), 2 usage error,
+3 unreadable file, 4 query matched nothing.
